      <p class="text-sm text-text-muted mb-4">July 17, 2015</p>
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-heading font-bold text-text-primary">
        Enterprise Planning &amp;amp; Forecasting Flow
      </h1>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 max-w-3xl prose-archive">
      <p>I was asked to show how all of the part of an organization's budgeting, planning and forecasting come together and support each other, and how the organization can get more sophisticated at forecasting.  This diagram helped explain the overall flow as well as some of the elements you would want to put on a roadmap.</p>

<p><a href="https://rondimon.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/07/enterprise-planning-flow.png"><img class="aligncenter size-large wp-image-192" src="/images/archive/enterprise-planning-flow.png" alt="enterprise planning flow" width="660" height="334" /></a></p>

<p>This should be a good starting place to have a debate about using the right planning and forecasting for better insight into the business, better resource deployment, and better profitability decision-making.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

</Page>
